{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "our ADK support agent on Cloud Run takes like 6-9 seconds before the first token streams back to the user, and it's way worse after the service has been idle for a bit. min-instances is 0 right now because finance yelled at us last quarter. can you help me figure out what's actually eating that time (container startup? model init? the tool registry loading?) and what we can change without blowing up the bill? demo to the client is next thursday"},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Hi — I'm running a multi-agent ADK app on GKE (Autopilot, us-central1) with a HorizontalPodAutoscaler on CPU at 70%. Two problems I'd like help with. First, long sessions get noticeably slower: by turn 30 or so each response takes 3x longer than at turn 1, and our Vertex AI token spend per session climbs with it. I suspect we're resending the full event history every turn, but I haven't confirmed it. Second, during morning traffic spikes the HPA scales up too late, so users get timeouts for a few minutes. Pods also sit at around 15% CPU most of the day, which seems wasteful. I'd like a way to instrument this properly (Cloud Trace? custom metrics?) so I can show my lead before/after numbers rather than guess. Session state is in Firestore, if that matters."},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "ugh. deployed my ADK agent to Cloud Run and now every request after the first one is super slow and then it 503s. logs show 'google.auth.exceptions.RefreshError' and something about the service account missing aiplatform.user. worked fine locally with my gcloud creds. what am i doing wrong", "needs_instead": "This is a deployment permissions and authentication problem, not performance tuning. The Cloud Run service account needs the right IAM roles, such as roles/aiplatform.user, and the credential setup needs fixing. The slowness is a symptom of failing auth retries, not something to profile."}
]}
